# Obelisk ISO package set.
#
# Phase 1 scope: a live medium that boots to a text console under both BIOS and UEFI.
# The desktop (Plasma 6), the installer (Calamares), and the Obelisk packages arrive in
# later phases. Every name below was verified against archlinux.org/packages; nothing
# here is guessed.
#
# Decision D1 (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md): the Windows compatibility layer, the VM stack,
# graphics drivers, and codecs are deliberately NOT on this medium. The first-run
# wizard fetches them after install. That is what keeps the ISO inside 3.5 GB and out
# of the way of the licensing rules in docs/LEGAL.md.

# --- base system -----------------------------------------------------------
base
linux
linux-lts
linux-firmware

# --- initramfs -------------------------------------------------------------
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
mkinitcpio-nfs-utils

# --- boot loaders ----------------------------------------------------------
# syslinux serves BIOS, grub serves UEFI. See bootmodes in profiledef.sh.
syslinux
grub
efibootmgr
edk2-shell

# --- memory diagnostics ----------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT. Resolved in Phase 2 rather than left open to Phase 4.
#
# The memtest boot entry came from releng's archiso_tail.cfg, which Obelisk no longer
# inherits: the boot menu is generated from design/tokens.yaml and contains exactly what
# we author. memtest86+ installs a kernel image at /boot/memtest86+/memtest that is only
# ever reachable from a boot loader entry, so with no entry the packages would ship
# 144 KiB that nothing on the medium can launch.
#
# Shipping a package nothing can start is worse than not shipping it. If Phase 4 decides
# a diagnostics entry earns a place in the five-entry live menu -- a fair argument, since
# Obelisk targets aging hardware where failing RAM is common and misdiagnosed -- the
# packages return together with the entry, not before it.


# --- filesystems -----------------------------------------------------------
# btrfs-progs is not optional: the whole unbreakability model in Phase 6 is Btrfs.
btrfs-progs
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
exfatprogs
f2fs-tools
xfsprogs
ntfs-3g

# --- partitioning ----------------------------------------------------------
gptfdisk
parted

# --- networking ------------------------------------------------------------
networkmanager
wireless-regdb

# --- installation tooling --------------------------------------------------
arch-install-scripts
pacman-contrib

# --- console usability -----------------------------------------------------
# The live console must be usable before any desktop exists, and terminus-font is
# what makes a HiDPI console readable at all.
terminus-font
nano
less
sudo
which
